<title>SINGAPORE: Seagate plans US$1 bln capital investments.</title>
<headline>Seagate plans US$1 bln capital investments.</headline>
<text>
<p>SINGAPORE, Feb 14 (REUTER) - Seagate Technology will spend more than US$1 billion in capital investment worldwide in 1997, Joel Stead, vice president/managing director sales and marketing Asia Pacific, said on Friday.  </p>
<p>&quot;This year we will invest more than US$1 billion in capital investments, with more than 70 percent into Asia Pacific,&quot; Stead told reporters at a luncheon.</p>
<p>He said the company will continue to invest in new plants and fit-ups of existing plants in the Asia Pacific region.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
